<title>USA: HSN Inc Q1 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>HSN Inc Q1 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>						 1997   1996(a)  1996 (b)</p>
<p>				(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>Net Revenues</p>
<p> Home Shopping			  $261,418  $255,613	$--</p>
<p> Broadcasting			     12,294    11,430   10,730</p>
<p> Other					 5,839	  --	382</p>
<p> Total net revenues		    279,551   267,043   11,112</p>
<p>Operating Expenses</p>
<p> Cost of sales			   158,615   165,918	128</p>
<p> Other costs				76,568    75,946    5,899</p>
<p> Depreciation and amortization	20,959    21,588    3,458</p>
<p> Total operating expenses	    256,142   263,452    9,485</p>
<p> Operating profit			 23,409     3,591    1,627</p>
<p> Interest expense, net		 (5,680)  (10,739)  (1,793)</p>
<p> Other income (expense), net	 (3,230)     2,302	137</p>
<p> Total				     (8,910)   (8,437)  (1,656)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) before income taxes</p>
<p>  and minority interest		 14,499   (4,846)     (29)</p>
<p> Income tax expense		   (11,129)   (3,273)    (577)</p>
<p> Minority interest			   400     1,252	 --</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)		     3,770   (6,867)    (606)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>    common shares			 50,623    48,731    9,456</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss) per common share  .07     (.14)    (.06)</p>
<p> EBITDA				     44,368    25,179    5,085</p>
<p> Attributable EBITDA(c)		 43,634    24,520    5,085</p>
<p>	  (a) Pro forma results of operations are stated as if</p>
<p>the mergers with Home Shopping Network and Savoy occurred on January 1, 1996 and exclude the operations of the Savoy motion picture business and include preliminary purchase accounting adjustments.</p>
<p>	  (b) Represents the actual results of operations only</p>
<p>for Silver King Communications Inc.</p>
<p>	  (c) HSN Inc owns 50% of the common equity and 100% of</p>
<p>the voting stock of SF Broadcasting.  As a result of voting and management control, its operating results are consolidated with HSN Inc's operating results. Attributable EBITDA reflects 50 pct of SF Broadcasting's EBITDA based on HSN Inc's common equity ownership.</p>
